OpenTTD for @SYSTEM@ (amd64)

OpenTTD 15.3, translated from C++ to C and compiled with @SYSTEM@'s
own compilers (https://github.com/yrk-lab/ottd-p9).  This directory
has the game (6.openttd: a Plan 9 binary, before it is installed),
the data it needs (lang, ai, game, media, bin, baseset, with the
free base sets OpenGFX, OpenSFX and OpenMSX), an mkfile to install
it, the licences (doc) and OpenTTD's own README.md.  The binary is
@SYSTEM@'s: there is a bundle for 9front and one for 9legacy.

Run it in place

	cd openttd
	./6.openttd

from a rio window (the game takes the window; it may be resized),
or on the bare screen.  The game finds its data next to the binary.

Install it

	mk install

for yourself: the binary as $home/bin/$cputype/openttd, the data in
$home/lib/openttd.  For everyone (as the host owner):

	mk BIN=/$cputype/bin install

puts the data in /sys/lib/openttd.  mk uninstall (with the same BIN)
takes it away again.  Then run openttd.

Where things go

$home/lib/openttd is the game's own directory: its configuration
(openttd.cfg), saved games (save), screenshots, and what it
downloads; it is also searched for data, as /sys/lib/openttd is.

Sound and music (9front)

The sound goes to /dev/audio; without a sound card (no /dev/audio:
bind -a '#A' /dev, or audio0= in plan9.ini) the game is silent.
The music is MIDI, played with games/dmid and games/opl3 and the
instrument bank of the Doom WAD 9front comes with
(/sys/games/lib/doom/doom1.wad).  A different bank, a GENMIDI lump
as a file named genmidi, can be put in a baseset directory.

On 9legacy

There is no sound (no audio device on amd64), and the keyboard gives
characters only, not keys going down and up: a held arrow key does
not scroll the map (drag with the right button, or use the arrows
one press at a time).

A server

	./6.openttd -D

is a dedicated server on port 3979; other OpenTTD 15.3 games (on
any system) can join it.  Its console reads the server's standard
input: type commands in its window (save x, quit), or pipe them in.

Notes

- The text is drawn with OpenTTD's own TrueType fonts (FreeType,
  linked in).  Game Options, Graphics, "Use traditional sprite font"
  switches to the built-in sprite font.
- The game loop, map generation, saving and the link graph run in
  threads of their own (Plan 9 processes: ps -a shows them by name).
- The interrupt (Del in a rio text window, or a note) asks the game
  to quit, as Ctrl+Q does; Del in the game's window closes its
  windows, as in OpenTTD elsewhere.  Web links are plumbed.
- The first start asks whether to take part in the survey: there is
  no web access here, nothing is ever sent; answer No.
- Saves of other OpenTTD 15.x games load, compressed or not.

